From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:24:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [voicecall] Only use Q_MOC_INCLUDE on Qt 6.

Q_MOC_INCLUDE first appeared in Qt 6.0, but the Qt 6 support guarded it
with Qt 5.15, so the tree no longer built against Qt 5.15:

  abstractvoicecallhandler.h:31:14: error: expected constructor,
  destructor, or type conversion before '(' token

Qt 5's moc does not need it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 lib/src/abstractvoicecallhandler.h         | 4 ++--
 plugins/declarative/src/voicecallhandler.h | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/src/abstractvoicecallhandler.h b/lib/src/abstractvoicecallhandler.h
index 56aac08..6245e5b 100644
--- a/lib/src/abstractvoicecallhandler.h
+++ b/lib/src/abstractvoicecallhandler.h
@@ -25,9 +25,9 @@
 #include <QDateTime>
 #include <QtGlobal>
 
-#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 15, 0)
+#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0)
 // moc needs to know where the forward-declared type lives to generate the
-// property metacalls; before 5.15 it found it via the old include scan.
+// property metacalls. The macro is new in Qt 6; Qt 5 moc did without it.
 Q_MOC_INCLUDE("abstractvoicecallprovider.h")
 #endif
 
diff --git a/plugins/declarative/src/voicecallhandler.h b/plugins/declarative/src/voicecallhandler.h
index 87524bd..431c2e2 100644
--- a/plugins/declarative/src/voicecallhandler.h
+++ b/plugins/declarative/src/voicecallhandler.h
@@ -5,9 +5,9 @@
 #include <QDateTime>
 #include <QtGlobal>
 
-#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 15, 0)
+#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0)
 // moc needs to know where the forward-declared type lives to generate the
-// property metacalls; before 5.15 it found it via the old include scan.
+// property metacalls. The macro is new in Qt 6; Qt 5 moc did without it.
 Q_MOC_INCLUDE("voicecallmodel.h")
 #endif
 
